# est_calib pins — REAL tokenizer counts of ripwire's output on test/estcalibfix.
# label o200k cl100k est_at_pin_time argv...   (space-separated; no argv may contain a space)
# Regenerate: python3 bench/tokenaudit/pin.py --bin build/ripwire   (needs tiktoken)
# Read by: test/tokenbudgetcheck.sh #18 — the calibration band. See bench/tokenaudit/README.md.
# RE-PINNED 2026-09-19 (lane/r2-namehits, LB3x round-2 lever): for-named ONLY, 789/785/1050 -> 959/954/1284.
# Attributed: base binary (origin/integration/train-7 @3bd3e8ae, unmodified) on this SAME fixture already
# reads 898/893/1195 for for-named and byte-identical numbers to this file's other seven rows — the
# other rows' drift from their pinned values (map 1009->974 etc.) predates this lane and is out of its
# scope. The remaining for-named delta (898->959 o200k, +61 B tokenized) is namehits.h's <namehits> append
# (default --for regime only), the only new bytes this lane's change adds to any pinned probe's output.

map 1009 999 1123 
map-topk5 538 535 653 --top-k=5
metrics 2381 2370 2509 --metrics
pack-signatures 1801 1784 2116 --pack-signatures
expand 541 542 455 --expand=billableTotal
for-named 959 954 1284 --for=billableTotal
for-budgeted 419 415 598 --for=dedupe --token-budget=400
pack-task 882 862 1104 --pack-task=dedupe
